factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The reel_script says the event was held at 'நாமக்கல் - திருச்சி சாலை ஸ்ரீமஹால்' — this matches the article, so no problem there; however the reel_script attributes the 'six months or yearly' advice and the 'kidney, heart' warning to Dr. Senthilkumar, who is the general manager, not a doctor — the article does state he said it, so this is acceptable.
  The reel_script states Dr. Gautam said 40-60 year olds should check eye power; the article attributes this to the chief doctor Gautam, which matches.
  The caption's headline sentence 'நாமக்கல் மருத்துவர் அறிவுரை' and the reel_script's claim that the three organisations 'jointly conducted' the event are supported, but the reel_script omits the key fact that the free check-up was given to all attendees at the event itself, which the article states ('அனைவருக்கும் இலவசமாக கண் பரிசோதனை செய்யப்பட்டது'); instead it only mentions the later free check-up for members, leaving out this important result.
  The reel_script says the eye check-up is needed 'for people above 40' in its opening sentence, but the article's central advice concerns those over 40 generally; the specific 40-60 age instruction is attributed to Dr. Gautam, so the phrasing 'நாமக்கல்லில் 40 வயதுக்கு மேற்பட்டோர் கண் பரிசோதனை செய்வது அவசியம் என மருத்துவர்கள் அறிவுறுத்தினர்' is consistent with the article.
